  {
   "id": "math-0016",
   "bucket": "reasoning",
   "planned_path": "P5",
   "scion_answer": "Using the binomial probability formula:\n\n$$P(X = k) = \\binom{n}{k} p^k (1-p)^{n-k}$$\n\nwhere $n = 5$, $p = \\frac{2}{3}$, and $k = 2$:\n\n**Step 1:** Compute the binomial coefficient:\n$$\\binom{5}{2} = \\frac{5!}{2! \\cdot 3!} = \\frac{120}{2 \\cdot 6} = 10$$\n\n**Step 2:** Compute the powers:\n$$\\left(\\frac{2}{3}\\right)^2 = \\frac{4}{9}, \\quad \\left(\\frac{1}{3}\\right)^3 = \\frac{1}{27}$$\n\n**Step 3:** Multiply:\n$$P(X = 2) = 10 \\cdot \\frac{4}{9} \\cdot \\frac{1}{27} = \\frac{40}{243}$$\n\n$$\\boxed{\\frac{40}{243}}$$",
