   "scion_answer": "```python\ndef even_odd_count(num):\n    \"\"\"Given an integer. return a tuple that has the number of even and odd digits respectively.\n\n     Example:\n        even_odd_count(-12) ==> (1, 1)\n        even_odd_count(123) ==> (1, 2)\n    \"\"\"\n    abs_num = abs(num)\n    digits = str(abs_num)\n    even_count = 0\n    odd_count = 0\n    for digit in digits:\n        if int(digit) % 2 == 0:\n            even_count += 1\n        else:\n            odd_count += 1\n    return (even_count, odd_count)\n```",
